# SRG-APP-000358-AU-000100  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must be configured to off-load log records onto a
# different system or media than the system being audited.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000358-AU-000100
group:           V-206491
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      tested
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001851
control_rev5:    AU-4

contribution:    Splunk off-loads log records through outputs.conf, where the target group
                 names the receiving systems, and that naming is the whole of the
                 application's share.

governs:         outputs.conf - Where this instance forwards its data, and how that connection is
                 protected.

check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] server non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] server https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/outputs.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The receiving indexer or external repository and its own inputs.conf -
                 SPLK-CL-000150 places that configuration on a separate machine, "which is
                 always a separate machine regardless of environment"
external:        The requirement's own not-applicable clause where an external application
                 or the operating system performs the off-load
external:        Where a target group uses indexerDiscovery instead of a static server
                 list, the cluster manager that supplies the receivers

citation:        outputs.conf [tcpout] defaultGroup non_empty is a false finding.
                 outputs.conf.spec:63-70 states "If you don't want to forward data
                 automatically, don't configure this setting", that it is overridden by
                 _TCP_ROUTING in inputs.conf, and that "Starting with version 4.2, this
                 setting is no longer required" - so a deployment that routes per input
                 forwards correctly with no defaultGroup at all. The setting also appears
                 in neither the check text nor the fix text, and in no checks.tsv row for
                 this requirement. One caution on the condition kept: outputs.conf.spec:128
                 makes server "Required if the 'indexerDiscovery' setting is not set", so a
                 target group that discovers its receivers satisfies the requirement
                 without it. The vocabulary has no way to express that alternative, so it
                 is recorded as an external dependency and the assessor must accept
                 indexerDiscovery as equivalent.
finding:         No forwarding target group names a receiving system, so the application is
                 not configured to off-load its log records to another system.
